\nand state Pollution Control Boards/Pollution Control Committees in Judgement dated \n20.07.2018 in oA No. 247/2017 to ensure implementation of PwM Rules, 2016 as \namended in 2018.\n\n150 Written Answers to [RAJyA sABHA] Unstarred Questions\nProject Elephant\n804.\t SHRI\t MD.\t NADIMUL\t HAQUE:\t Will\t the\t Minister\t of\t ENVIRONMENT,\t\nfoResT ANd ClIMATe CHANge be pleased to state:\n(a) whether Project elephant is being poorly funded and has minimal staff;\n(b) if so, the state/uT-wise details thereof along with the reasons therefor;\n(c) if not, the details of funds allocated, released and utilised along with the \nstaff deployed per elephant for conservation during last three years, state/uT-wise;\n(d) the deaths of elephants during the above period along with the causes of \ntheir deaths, state/uT-wise;\n(e)\t the\t deaths\t of\t humans\t due\t to\t the\t human-elephant\t conflicts\t during\t the\t above\t\nperiod, state/uT-wise; and\n(f) whether government has issued any guidelines for managing human-elephant \nconflict,\t if\t so,\t the\t details\t thereof?\nTHe MINIsTe R of sTATe  IN THe  MINIsTR y  of eNvIRoNMe NT, foResT \nANd ClIMATe CHANge (dR. MAHesH sHARMA): (a) No, sir.\n(b) does not arise.\n(c) The state-wise details of funds allocated, released and utilized under the \nscheme Project elephant during last three years are given in the statement-I (See \nbelow).\n(d) The death of elephant due to various reasons like train accident, electrocution, \npoaching and poisoning during the last three years, state-wise, is given in statement-II, \nIII, Iv  and v  respectively (See below).\n(e)\t The\t details\t of\t human\t deaths\t due\t to\t human-elephant\t conflict\t during\t the\t last\t\nthree years, state-wise, is given in the statement-vI (See below).\n(f) y es, sir. The Ministry vide letter dated 6.0.2017 has issued a detailed \nGuidelines\t for\t Management\t of\t Human-Elephant\t Conflict\t to\t all\t the\t elephant\t range\t\nstates for implem