Km. 185/500 to Km. 215/480 excluding  \nKm. 205/180 to Km. 210/900 of NH 183 (old NH 220)\n24.26 33.76 21.04.2018 20.04.2019 60\n22. Construction of Pathiri bridge at Km. 89/400 on NH 766 (old \nNH 212)\n- 5.23 01.02.2017 31.01.2018/ \n31.03.2019\n85\n23. Reconstruction of Kazhuthurutty Bridge at Km. 69/960 of NH-744 - 3.43 12.10.2015 11.07.2016/ \n31.03.2019\n78\n24. Reconstruction of Muruganpanchal Bridge at Km. 76/00 of \nNH-744\n- 3.39 02.10.2015 11.07.2016/ \n31.03.2019\n85\n\n214 Written Answers to [RAJyA sABHA] Unstarred Questions\nExpansion of Gutti-Tadipatri Highway\n841. sHRI T. g. veNKATesH: w ill the Minister of RoAd TRANsPoRT ANd \nHIgHw Ays be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Ministry has given its acceptance to the expansion of gutti-\nTadipatri Highway into a four lane road and if so, the details thereof; \n(b) the details of quantum of funds being allocated for this expansion work; \nand \n(c)\t whether\t any\t time-frame\t has\t been\t fixed\t to\t complete\t the\t work,\t if\t so,\t the\t\ndetails thereof?\nTHe  MINI sT e R of sTAT e  IN THe  MINI sTRy  of R oAd TRANsPoRT \nANd HIgHw Ays (sHRI MANsuKH MANdA vIy A): (a) Ministry has sanctioned \nrehabilitation and upgradation of gooty-Tadipatri section of NH-67 from km 424/650 \nto km 487/693 to two lane with paved shoulders in the state of Andhra Pradesh. \nout of the total project length of 63.043 km, a length of 3.72 km is to be upgraded \nto four/six lane in built-up areas. \n(b) and (c) The sanctioned cost of the above project is ` 378.24 crore. The above \nwork has commenced on 19.01.2018 and scheduled date of completion is 18.01.2020. \nConstruction of Highways in Uttar Pradesh\n842. sHRIMATI CHHA yA veRMA: \n  sHRI vIsHAMBHAR PRAsAd NIsHAd:  \n  CH. suKHRAM sINgH yAdAv :\nw ill the Minister of RoAd TRANsPoRT ANd HIgHw Ays be pleased to state:\n(a) the status of the construction work of gorakhpur-Kushinagar four lane, \ngorakhpur-v aranasi four lane and Kalesar to Jungle Kaudiya four lane bypass; \n(b) the status of other, under construction roads of uttar Pradesh;\n(c) the date of announcement for the construction of these roads and the target \nfor their completion; \n(d) whether it is a fact that construction of these roads is far, from its set target; \n(e) whether the construction cost of these roads have been raised or is being \ncontemplated to be raised due to this delay; and \n(f) the reasons for the delay in construction work of the said roads?\n\nWritten Answers to [11 february, 2019]   Unstarred Questions 215\nTHe  MINI sT e R of sTAT e  IN THe  MINI sTRy  of R oAd TRANsPoRT \nANd HIgHw Ays (sHRI MANsuKH MANdA vIy A): (a) four-laning of gorakhpur-\nKushinagar (86.317 Km.) has been completed. four-laning of varanasi-gorakhpur \n(203 Km.) and four-laning of gorakhpur bypass (Kalesar to Jungle Kaudiya) are in \nimplementation stage.\n(b) to (f) Ministry of Road Transport and Highways is primarily responsible \nfor development and maintenance of National Highways in the country and it is a \ncontinuous\t process.\t The\t target\t set\t during\t the\t current\t financial\t year\t i.e. 2018-19, for \nconstruction of National Highways in the state of uttar Pradesh is 1023 km. out of \nwhich 607 km has already been constructed till January, 2019. The reasons for delay \nin highway projects are delay in land acquisition, shifting of utilities, environmental, \nforest clearances, railway approvals, poor performance of contractors, etc. In ePC \nand Item rate contract, there is a provision for payment of escalation due to delay. \nIn case the project is delayed due to reasons attributed to the contractor, liquidated \ndamages are to be imposed and no escalation is paid.\nWidening of NH-43 \n843. CH. suKHRAM sINgH yAdAv : \n  sHRIMATI CHHA yA veRMA: \n  sHRI vIsHAMBHAR PRAsAd NIsHAd:\nw ill the Minister of RoAd TRANsPoRT ANd HIgHw Ays be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the work of widening of the Katni to gumla section of National \nHighway No. 43, has been delayed;\n(b) if so, the reasons for delay in widening of the road and the action taken \nfor not adhering to time-line; and \n(c) whether the set standards for widening of road are being followed so that \nlocal people do not suffer? \nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe IN THe MINIsTR y  of RoAd TRANsPoRT ANd  \nHIgHw Ays (sHRI MANsuKH MANdA vIy A): (a) some works of widening of \nthe Katni to gumla section of National Highway (NH) No. 43, have been delayed.\n(b) The reason for delay in widening of the road and the action taken for not \nadhering to time-line are as under:–\n\n216 Written Answers to [RAJyA sABHA] Unstarred Questions\nsl. \nNo.\nstate Road stretch/No. of Projects delayed Projects Reasons for \ndelay\nAction taken \nfor completion \nof delayed \nprojects\n1. Madhya Pradesh Katni-umariya-shahdol-MP/Cg Border-There are \nthree projects. Projects from Katni to umariya \nand shahdol to MP/Cg Border has already \ncompleted.\n1. umariya-shadol Poor performance \nof contractor, \nland Acquisition \nand other issues \nincluding forest \nclearances.\nsub-contactor \nhas been engaged \nto expedite the \ncompletion of \nwork.\n2. Chhattisgarh MP/Cg Border-Mahendra Nagar-surjapur-\nAmbikapur-Pathalgaon-Kunkuri-Cg/Jharkhand \nBorder-out of seven projects, only two projects \nare delayed.\n1. Ambikapur-\n Pathalgaon-\n2. Pathalgaon-\n Kunkuri\nPoor performance \nof contractor, \nland Acquisition \nand other issues \nincluding forest \nclearances.\nsub-contactor \nhas been engaged \nto expedite the \ncompletion of \nwork.\n3. Jharkhand Cg/Jharkhand Border to gumla Nil Nil Nil\n(c) y es, sir.\n\nWritten Answers to [11 february, 2019]   Unstarred Questions 217\nConstruction of NHs in Bihar\n844. sHRI RAM NATH THAKuR: w ill the Minister of RoAd TRANsPoRT \nANd HIgHw Ays be pleased to state:\n(a) the amount allocated for the construction and repairing of National Highways \nin\t Bihar\t during\t the\t current\t financial\t year,\t National\t Highway-wise;\n(b) the progress made in the construction work of Buxar-Patna four lane NH \nand by when it would be completed; and\n(c) whether it is a fact that the construction work of this highway is sluggish due \nto land acquisition related hurdles and slow pace of work by construction company?\nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe IN THe MINIsTR y  of RoAd TRANsPoRT ANd  \nHIgHw Ays (sHRI MANsuKH MANdA vIy A): (a) The state-wise allocation is made \nfor the amount for the construction and repairing of National Highways under NH \n(o) and M&R. The amount allocated for the construction and repairing of National \nHighways\t to\t the\t State\t Government\t during\t the\t current\t financial\t year\t are\t ` 1846.31 \ncrore and ` 43.06 crore respectively. However, no state-wise allocation made for \nNational Highways under National Highways Authority of India (NHAI). NHAI has \nincurred ` 796.55 crore for construction and repairing of National Highways in Bihar \nduring\t the\t current\t financial\t year.\n(b) Construction work of Patna-Buxar section has been undertaken in 3 packages. \nstatus of current progress are as below:–\n1. Patna-Koilwar section: w ork is recommended for fore-closure for want \nof lA.\n2. Koilwar-Bhojpur section: Physical Progress-27.91%, Completion date-\n02.01.2020\n3. Bhojpur-Buxar section: Physical progress-7.51%, Completion date-16.10.2020\n(c) y es sir, The progress is behind the schedule due to land acquisition related \nhurdles and slow mobilization of contractor.\nSix-laning of NH-8\n845. KuMARI selJA: w ill the Minister of RoAd TRANsPoRT ANd  \nHIgHw Ays be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the travel-time from gurgaon to Jaipur due to the six-laning of NH-8 \nhas been reduced to three and a half hours as promised by the Ministry in 2016;\n\n218 Written Answers to [RAJyA sABHA] Unstarred Questions\n(b) if not, the reasons therefor and the details of hindrances faced;\n(c) whether the overbridges and underpasses have been built fully and are \noperational on the delhi-Jaipur stretch of NH-8, if not, the reasons therefor;\n(d) the details of accidents, fatal and otherwise which have taken place in the \nlast three years on NH-8 on the delhi-Jaipur stretch; and\n(e) the details of funds allocated and spent on the delhi-Jaipur stretch of NH-8?\nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe IN THe MINIsTR y  of RoAd TRANsPoRT ANd  \nHIgHw Ays (sHRI MANsuKH MANdA vIy A): (a) and (b) Presently, travel-time \nfrom gurgaon to Jaipur is approximately 4-4.5 hours. The concessionaire has not \nbeen attending to the maintenance works along with the balance work for which \nCure Period notice has already been issued to the concessionaire. further, separate \nbids for the maintenance work and balance work have been invited and these works \nare envisaged to be executed at the risk and cost of concessionaire.\n(c)\t The\t concessionaire\t had\t to\t construct\t 57\t nos.\t of\t structures\t (flyover/VUPs/\nPuPs etc.) out of which 56 nos. of structures are functional. The balance structure \nhas been envisaged to be constructed by separate agency at the risk and cost of \nconcessionaire.\n(d) during the last three years, the accidents have reduced by more than 40%. \nfurther, the fatal accidents have been reduced by about 25% during the last three \nyears.\n(e) The project for 6-laning of gurgaon-Jaipur stretch is a BoT(Toll) project for \nwhich concessionaire has to arrange funds at its own level. However, an amount of \n` 352 crores has been sanctioned under one-time fund infusion scheme to complete \nthe project at the earliest.\nPending construction of roads\n846. dR. AMee yAJNIK: w ill the Minister of RoAd TRANsPoRT ANd  \nHIgHw Ays be pleased to state\n(a) kilometre of roads constructed during the financial years 2015-16, 2016-17 \nand 2017-18, with a break-up of road, state-wise;\n(b)\t number\t of\t tenders\t floated\t and\t contracts\t awarded\t thereafter\t for\t the\t road\t\nconstruction during the said fys in the country;\n(c) length in kilometres of roads for which bidding process is still pending and \nthe total worth of these bids; and\n\nWritten Answers to [11 february, 2019]   Unstarred Questions 219\n(d) length in kilometres of roads pending for construction whose bidding process \nhave been completed during fys 2015-16, 2016-17 and 2017-18 and the total worth \nof these tenders for the road construction with break-up, state-wise?\nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe IN THe MINIsTR y  of RoAd TRANsPoRT ANd  \nHIgHw Ays (sHRI MANsuKH MANdA vIy A): (a) The state-wise construction of \nNational Highways (NHs) during the financial years 2015-16, 2016-17 and 2017-18 \nis given in the statement-I (See below). \n(b) About 43,101 km of contracts were tendered and then awarded during the \nfys 2015-16, 2016-17 and 2017-18. \n(c) Ministry has invited bids of worth 6708 km as on 31st January in the \ncurrent\t financial\t year\t 2018-19.\t\n(d) As the awarding and completion of NHs projects is a continuous process, \nthe state-wise details of length awarded and completed during the last three fys is \ngiven in the statement-II.\nStatement-I\nState/UT-wise details of length of NHs constructed  \nduring each of the last three years\nsl. \nNo.\nstate/uT length completed (in km)\n2015-16 2016-17 2017-18\n1   2 3 4 5\n1. Andhra Pradesh 462 402 459\n2. Arunachal Pradesh 80 174 188\n3. Assam 87 165 305\n4. Bihar 181 400 343\n5. Chandigarh 0 0 0\n6. Chhattisgarh 327 483 522\n7. delhi 0 0 139\n8. goa 2 4 20\n9. gujarat 277 86 189\n10. Haryana 170 369 291\n11. Himachal Pradesh 100 72 135\n12. Jammu and Kashmir 34 33 162\n\n220 Written Answers to [RAJyA sABHA] Unstarred Questions\n1   2 3 4 5\n13. Jharkhand 119 211 238\n14. Karnataka 314 656 769\n15. Kerala 10 46 16\n16. Madhya Pradesh 306 475 594\n17. Maharashtra 324 750 1,338\n18. Manipur 6 4 231\n19. Meghalaya 50 6 48\n20. Mizoram 15 88 43\n21. Nagaland 25 4 4\n22. odisha 268 490 554\n23. Puducherry 22 8 17\n24. Punjab 154 384 357\n25. Rajasthan 1,063 1,125 1,074\n26. sikkim 0 0 45\n27. Tamil Nadu 237 46