n \nsevoke at Km. 592.40 of NH-31.\n16. Construction of 4-lane RoB (Twins 2-lanes) and its approaches in replacement \nof level crossing at Km. 3.950 of NH-2B (Railway Km. 226/0) at Talit.\n17. Construction of RoB and its approaches in lieu  of level Crossing at Km. \n661.00 on NH-31 (Maynaguri).\n\n238 Written Answers to [RAJyA sABHA] Unstarred Questions\nsl.No. Name of Projects\n18. Construction of RoB and its approaches in lieu of level Crossing No. 1/T/\nsPl  (at Barasat Kazipara) at Km. 3.25 on NH-35.\n19. Construction of twins 2-lane RoB and its approaches in replacement of existing \nlevel crossing gate No.-38 (Rly Km. 165/21-165/23) between Chondrakona \nRoad and garbeta stations in Kadamdiha at Km. 159.448 of NH-60.\nStatement-III\nList of the projects that are being planned for being launched in next one year\nsl.No. Name of Projects\n1. dalkhola-Islampur-siliguri-salsalabari (ew)\n2. ghoshpukur-Kharibari-Bhajanpur-Araria (with spur to Panitanki and Kishangarh)\n3. Kharagpur-siliguri (Till Morgram)\n4. Kharagpur-Kolkata eXP\n5. Barasat-Krishnanagar\nToilet complexes at Toll Booths\n856. sHRIMATI vIPlove THAKuR: w ill the Minister of RoAd TRANsPoRT \nANd HIgHw Ays be pleased to state:\n(a) whether National Highways Authority of India (NHAI) has any proposal to \nconstruct toilet complexes and kiosks at every toll booth on the National Highways, \nif so, the details thereof;\n(b)\t whether\t NHAI\t has\t any\t proposal\t to\t station\t ambulances\t and\t fire\ttenders\t at\t the\t\ntoll booths to press them into service in the event of an accident on the National \nHighways; and\n(c) if so, the details thereof and the current status of the scheme? \nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe IN THe MINIsTR y  of RoAd TRANsPoRT ANd  \nHIgHw Ays (sHRI MANsuKH MANdA vIy A): (a) NHAI is constructing Highway \nNest (Mini) on up/down side of toll plazas for convenience of highway users for \ntheir safe and comfortable journey. It has toilets, kiosk for sale of dry snacks, tea \nand coffee vending machine and water ATM etc. Also there is provision of toilets \nat all toll plazas of NHAI.\n(b) and (c) As part of incident management under operation and maintenance of \nthe NH stretches, highway ambulances are deployed in their respective service area \nto extend assistance in case of any emergency on National Highways.\n\nWritten Answers to [11 february, 2019]   Unstarred Questions 239\nVillages adopted under Adarsh Gram Yojana\n857. sHRI RA vI PRAKAsH veRMA: \n  sHRI NeeRAJ sHeKHAR:\nw ill the Minister of RuRAl  develoPMeNT be pleased to state:\n(a) the details of criteria for declaration of a village as Adarsh gram under \nAdarsh gram y ojana;\n(b) the details of villages adopted as Adarsh gram under the scheme during \n2018-19 till 31st January, 2019;\n(c) the details of adopted villages developed as Adarsh gram during 2018-19 \ntill date, as per the above criteria, state-wise; and\n(d) the details of villages developed as Adarsh grams in uttar Pradesh so far, \ndistrict-wise and year-wise since 2014 till date?\nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe IN THe MINIsTR y  of RuRAl  develoPMeNT \n(sHRI RAM KRIPAl  yAdAv): (a) and (c) An Adarsh gram evolves out of people’s \nshared vision, using their capacities and available resources to the best extent possible, \nduly facilitated by the Hon’ble Member of Parliament, the gram Panchayat, civil \nsociety and the government machinery. The elements of an Adarsh gram are context \nspecific.\t The\t Gram\t Panchayats\t adopted\t under\t SAGY\t prepare\t Village\t Development\t\nPlans (vdP) through a participatory process under the guidance of Hon’ble Members \nof Parliament. The vdP includes prioritised time-bound activities to achieve holistic \nprogress\t of\t the\t village.\t Out\t of\t the\t 1,471\t Gram\t Panchayats\t identified\t under\t SAGY ,\t\n1,206 gram Panchayats have uploaded their vdPs containing 65,252 projects, as per \ndata available on sAgy  website (http://saanjhi.gov.in) on 6th february, 2019 and \nimplementation of 33,428 (51%) projects has been completed. The details of adopted \nvillages developed as Adarsh gram during 2018-19 till date, as per the above criteria, \nstate-wise are given in the statement-I (See below).\n(b) The details of villages adopted as Adarsh gram under the scheme during \n2018-19 till 31st January, 2019 are given in the statement-II (See below).\n(d) The details of villages developed as Adarsh grams in uttar Pradesh so far, \ndistrict-wise and year-wise since 2014 till date given in the statement-III.\n\n240 Written Answers to [RAJyA sABHA] Unstarred Questions\nStatement-I\nDetails of adopted villages developed as Adarsh Gram during 2018-19, \nState-wise as on 6th February, based on the information uploaded \nby the State on the SAGY portal (saanjhi.gov.in)\nsl.\nNo.\nName of the state/uT Name of the district Name of the gram \nPanchayat\n1    2 3 4\n1. Andaman and Nicobar \nIslands\nsouth Andamans w andoor\n2. Andhra Pradesh sPsR Nellore Pallipadu\n3. Assam Chirang Barpathar\ndhubri Anandanagar Bangalipara\ngoalpara dhanubhanga\n4. Bihar samastipur Pagra\nsamastipur Nawachak\nPashchim Champaran Patilar\ngaya Nawan\ngaya Mahuyet\nsheohar dhankaul\nBuxar sonbarsa\nBuxar Khutahan\nRohtas gunsej\n5. Chhattisgarh Balod latabore\nJashpur Bagbahar\nKorba dhavaipur\ndurg Amleshwar\ngariyaband Munghjhar\nBalrampur Kakana\ndhamtari Ranwa\n6. delhi North w est delhi salahpur Majra\nNorth w est delhi Budhanpur Majra\n\nWritten Answers to [11 february, 2019]   Unstarred Questions 241\n1 2 3 4\nNorth delhi singola\n7. goa North goa Querim\n8. gujarat Mahesana Mandalikharod\nRajkot Mota gundala\nKheda Piplag\ngandhinagar Pansar\nBanas Kantha sundha\nKachchh Nirona\nRajkot Kamlapur\n9. Haryana faridabad Chhainsa\nBhiwani Chehar Khurd\n10. Himachal Pradesh shimla Balog\nKangra Chachian Khas\nBilaspur Kothi\nMandi simas\n11. Jammu and Kashmir doda Hambal-a\n12. Karnataka udupi Kadur\nBangalore Rural giddappanahalli\nChitradurga Kunubevu\nRaichur guntagol