s\n  1    2    3\nlucknow Bahru\nsakra\nMaharajganj gonha\nMainpuri Bamhauri Awahar\ndudgaun\nMathura Managarhi\nPentha\nMau Barbochi\nMeerut Bahadurpur\nJarauda\nMirzapur Baghi\nMoradabad guaroo\nPalupura ghosi\nMuzaffarnagar Pipalshah\nPilibhit Pandari\nPratapgarh Jagdishpur\nRampur Mathurapur\nNankar Rani\nPatti Kalan\nsaharanpur sabbipur\nsambhal Rehtol\nsant Kabeer Nagar umila\nsant Ravidas Nagar lagan Bari\nshahjahanpur v ikrampur\nKhajuri\nNabhichi\nshamli Buchha Kheri\nsiddharth Nagar lotan\nsitapur Humaunpur\nIslam Nagar\n\nWritten Answers to [11 february, 2019]   Unstarred Questions 259\n  1    2    3\nsahiapur\nsonbhadra dareva\nunnao Behata Kachh\nfatehpur Chaorasi gramin\nvaranasi Kakarhia\nRamna\n2018 Allahabad Chikhari\ndelaunha\nAmbedkar Nagar semur Khanpur\nAmroha Kankather\nBallia Keharpur\nMirzapur\nsahulai Hardo Patti\nBarabanki Peend\netah shakrauli\netawah Barra\nfaizabad sunwa\nghaziabad Mewala Bhatti\nMilak Chakarpur\nNagla firoj Mohanpur\nHamirpur Niwada\nKanpur Nagar Baikunh Pur\nsapai\nKheri Moodi\nlucknow durjanpur\nMaharajganj semrahwa\nMirzapur devri uttar\nMoradabad Mohra\nPilibhit Bhadeg Kanja\nPratapgarh dharupur\n\n260 Written Answers to [RAJyA sABHA] Unstarred Questions\n  1    2    3\nKatra Indra Kunwar\nPurekisuni\nsiddharth Nagar Pendari Buzurg\nvaranasi domari\nRoopchandpur\nDeen Dayal Antyodaya Yojana\n858. sHRI PRABHAT JHA: w ill the Minister of RuRAl  develoPMeNT be \npleased to state:\n(a) whether the purpose of d een dayal Antyodaya yojana-Rashtriya g ramin \nAajeevika Mission is to ensure access to eight to nine crore poor rural families and \nconnect one woman member of each family with women self Help groups (sHgs) \nand unions whose relatives are working at rural level and higher levels;\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether the progress made so far in the aforesaid purpose of deen dayal \nAntyodaya yojana-Rashtriya gramin Aajeevika Mission is progressing as per its target; \nand\n(d) if so, the details thereof?\nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe IN THe MINIsTR y  of RuRAl  develoPMeNT \n(sHRI RAM KRIPAl  yAdAv): (a) and (b) The focus of deen dayal Antodaya \ny ojana-National Rural livelihoods Mission (dA y-NRlM) is eradication of rural \npoverty through building institutions of the poor women and enabling them to \naccess\t a\t range\t of\t financial,\t livelihoods\t and\t convergence\t services.\t The\t programme\t\naims to bring at least one woman member from each rural poor household, as per \nthe socio economic Caste Census (seCC) 2011 data, into the fold of self Help \ngroups (sHgs) formed under the programme by reaching out to 8-10 crore poor \nhouseholds by the year 2023-24.\n(c) and (d) As of december, 2018 about 5.68 crore households have been \nmobilized\t into\t 49.89\t lakh\t SHGs.\t The\t total\t financial\t support\t provided\t to\t the\t SHGs\t\ntill december, 2018 in the form of Community Investment support fund (CIsf) and \nRevolving fund (Rf) amounts to ` 6058.64 crores.\n\nWritten Answers to [11 february, 2019]   Unstarred Questions 261\nCurbing Rural Migration Rate\n859. sHRI RAKesH sINHA: w ill the Minister of RuRAl  develoPMeNT \nbe pleased to state:\n(a) details of rural migration rate during the year 2014-15, 2015-16 and 2017-18;\n(b) measures taken by government to curb rural migration; and\n(c) name of ten states from where rural migration is highest and the comparative \nrate of rural migration in these states?\nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe IN THe MINIsTR y  of RuRAl  develoPMeNT \n(SHRI\t RAM\t KRIPAL\tY ADA V):\t(a)\t to\t (c)\t National\t Sample\t Survey\t Office\t(NSSO)\t has\t\nnot conducted survey on migration during 2014-15, 2015-16 and 2017-18. However, \nNational\t Sample\t Survey\t Office\t (NSSO)\t in\t its\t 64th\t Sample\t Survey\t conducted\t during\t\nJuly, 2007 to June, 2008 collected migration particulars along with the information on \nemployment and unemployment. The percentage distribution of migrants by reason for \nmigration obtained from the survey on ‘employment and u nemployment and Migration \nParticulars’ conducted by Nsso during 2007-08 is given in statement (See below).\nMinistry of Rural development is implementing various rural development \nschemes for creating employment opportunities, providing access to basic needs and \ncreating rural infrastructure. Mahatma gandhi National Rural employment guarantee \nScheme\t provides\t guaranteed\t wage\t employment\t of\t 100\t days\t in\t a\t financial\t year\t\nto a rural household whose adult members are willing to take up manual work. \ndeendayal Antyodaya yojana-National Rural livelihoods Mission (dA y-NRlM) is \nimplemented with the objective of providing self-employment to the members of the \nrural\t poor\t families.\t The\t findings\t of\t Independent\t studies\t conducted\t by\t the\t Ministry\t\nof Rural development indicate that out-migration from villages has gone down due \nto implementation of Mahatma gandhi NRegs. The department is implementing \nshyama Prasad Mukherji Rurban Mission (sPMRM) aimed at developing 300 rural \ngrowth clusters called ‘Rurban Clusters’ which have latent potential for growth, in \nall states and uTs. The objective of the Mission is to bridge the rural urban divide \nand to reduce migration from rural to urban areas and eventually to facilitate reverse \nmigration. Besides, Pradhan Mantri Awaas yojana-gramin (PMA y-g) and Pradhan \nMantri gram sadak yojana (PMgsy) are also implemented to provide basic needs \nand developing rural infrastructure for improving living conditions of rural masses \nso that distress migration of people from rural to cities could be reduced.\n\n262 Written Answers to [RAJyA sABHA] Unstarred Questions\nStatement\nPercentage distribution of migrants (in 0.0) by reason for migration obtained from \nthe survey on ‘Employment and Unemployment and Migration Particulars’  \nconducted by NSSO during 2007-08\nsl. \nNo.\nReason for migration Rural urban\nMale female Male female\nAll-India\n1. In search of employment 4.6 0.1 15.1 0.6\n2. In search of better employment 9.6 0.2 16.5 0.6\n3. Business 1.7 0.0 3.0 0.1\n4. To take up employment/better \nemployment\n8.1 0.2 13.3 0.9\n5. Transfer of service/contract 3.6 0.1 6.8 0.3\n6. Proximity to place of work 1.0 0.1 1.0 0.2\n7. studies 10.7 0.5 6.8 2.2\n8. Natural disaster 1.2 0.1 0.2 0.1\n9. social/political problem 2.4 0.2 0.7 0.3\n10. displacement by development \nprojects\n0.6 0.0 0.4 0.1\n11. Acquisition\t of\t own\t house/flat 4.2 0.3 3.4 0.9\n12. Housing problems 3.9 0.3 1.6 0.6\n13. Health care 1.1 0.1 0.4 0.2\n14. Post retirement 2.6 0.0 0.7 0.0\n15. Marriage 9.4 91.2 1.4 60.8\n16. Migration of parent/earning \nmember of the family\n22.1 4.4 25.2 29.4\n17. others 12.2 1.7 3.4 2.2\n18. All (incl. N.R.) 100.0 100.0 100.0 100.0\nNR: Not reported.\nNote:\n1. Migrant: A household member whose last usual place of residence (uPR), anytime in the past, \nwas different from the present place of enumeration  was considered as a migrant member of the \nhousehold.\n2.\t Usual\t place\t of\t residence:\t Usual\t place\t of\t residence\t (UPR)\t of\t a\t person\t was\t defined\tas\t a\t place\t (village/\ntown) where the person had stayed continuously for a period of six months or more.\nSource: Nss Report No. 553: Migration in India: July, 2007-June, 2008.\n\nWritten Answers to [11 february, 2019]   Unstarred Questions 263\nMGNREGA in Andhra Pradesh\n860. sHRI v. vIJAyAsAI Reddy : w ill the Minister of RuRAl  develoPMeNT \nbe pleased to state:\n(a) total amount allocated by the Ministry for MgNRegA to the state of Andhra \nPradesh during the last three years and the current year, year-wise;\n(b) details of household families that have sought employment and got employment \nunder MgNRegA during the above period, district-wise;\n(c) details of assets created, district-wise, during the above period;\n(d)  whether Ministry found any diversion/irregularities in implementation of \nMgNRegA in Andhra Pradesh and\n(e) if so, details thereof and action taken by the Ministry on the same?\nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe IN THe MINIsTR y  of RuRAl  develoPMeNT \n(sHRI RAM KRIPAl  yAdAv): (a) Mahatma gandhi National Rural employment \nguarantee Act, 2005 (MgNRegA) is a demand driven wage employment scheme, \nhence no state/u T-wise allocation of fund is made. As per the government of Andhra \nPradesh,\t the\t details\t of\t Central\t fund\t released\t during\t the\t last\t three\t financial\t years\t\nand\t the\t current\t financial\t year\t 2018-19\t (as\t on\t 05.02.2019)\t under\t the\t MGNREGA\t\nare given below:–\n(` in crore)\nfinancial year 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 (as on 05.02.2019)\nCentral fund released 2856.85 3997.46 5287.32 6420.94\n(b) As per the Management Information system (MIs), the district-wise details \nof employment demanded by households and employment offered to households \nduring\t the\t last\t three\t financial\t years\t and\t the\t current\t financial\t year\t 2018-19\t (as\t on\t\n07.02.2019) under the MgNRegA are given in the statement-I (See below).\n(c) As per the government of Andhra Pradesh, the district-wise details of assets \ncreated\t during\t the\t last\t three\t financial\t years\t and\t the\t current\t financial\t year\t 2018-19\t\n(as on 06.02.2019) under the MgNRegA are given in the statement-II (See below).\n(d) and (e) The Ministry, under MgNRegA receives complaints of diversion/\nirregularities in implementation of MgNRegA from states including Andhra Pradesh. \nsince the responsibility of implementation of MgNRegA is vested with the state \ngovernments/uTs, all complaints received in the Ministry are forwarded to the \nconcerned state governments/uTs for taking appropriate action including investigation, \nas per law.\n\n264 Written Answers to [RAJyA sABHA] Unstarred Questions\nStatement-I \nDistrict-wise details of employment demanded by households and employment \noffered to households during the last three financial years and \ncurrent fin