urpose Hall at Manpolyang, \nziro, lower, subansiri district\n8.00\n43. Madhya \nPradesh\nlaying of Astro Turf Hockey field at Railway \nstadium, gwalior, Madhya Pradesh\n2.90\nToT al 285.82\nStatement-II\nDetails of sports infrastructure projects sanctioned under PMDP  \nfor enhancement of sports infrastructure in Jammu and Kashmir\n(` in crore)\nsl.No. Projects Amount earmarked\n1. Renovation and development of Bakshi stadium and other \nworks\n44.00\n2. Renovation and development of M.A stadium and other works 40.00\n3. Construction of 22 Indoor Halls 88.00\n4. upgradation of existing sports stadia at Rajouri and Poonch 4.00\n5. Completion/upgradation of subash stadium at udhampur 10.00\n6. development of water sports infrastructure at Jammu and \nsrinagar\n6.00\n7. lighting system at TRC ground/gani stadium 2.63\n\nWritten Answers to [11 february, 2019]   Unstarred Questions 389\nSupport and encouragement for sports activities at global stage\n921. dR. l. HANuMANTHAIAH: w ill the Minister of youTH Aff AIRs ANd \nsPoRTs be pleased to state:\n(a) the details of remarkable achievements of our country in various sports \ndisciplines including track events on the global stage;\n(b) details of gold/silver medal and other category-wise medals won during the \nlast three years including current year, year-wise;\n(c) whether it is a fact that sportspersons of our country in various sports \nevents, including track events, are not given adequate support and encouragement \nto participate in sports activities held at global stage;\n(d) if so, details thereof; and\n(e) whether government is allocating adequate funds to promote sports and \ngames in the country?\nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe of THe MINIsTR y  of youTH Aff AIRs ANd \nsPoRTs (Col. RAJy AvARdHAN sINgH RATHoRe): (a) and (b) International \nsporting events, including track events, are organized by the world body concerned, \nin association with the International olympic Committee (IoC)/National olympic \nCommittee (NoC) concerned and the National level sports federations concerned. \nParticipation of Indian sportspersons in events on the global stage is primarily the \nresponsibility of the National level sports federations/NoCs concerned. Therefore, \ncomplete information on remarkable achievements of our country in various sports \ndisciplines including track events on the global stage is not maintained in this \nMinistry. However, details of Indian sportspersons who have won medals in olympics, \nCommonwealth games and Asian games during the last three years and the current \nyear, including in track events, is given in the statement-I (See below). In addition, \nMs.\t Hima\t Das,\t an\t Indian\t sprint\t runner\t was\t the\t first\t Indian\t athlete\t to\t win\t a\t gold\t\nmedal in a track event in 400m. at the IAAf w orld u20 Championships, 2018.\n(c) to (e) sports is a state subject and development of sports, including giving \nadequate support and encouragement to participate in sports activities held at global \nstage and allocation of adequate funds to promote sports and games in the country, is \nprimarily the responsibility of the state governments and National sports federations \nconcerned. This Ministry complements/supplements their efforts in this regard, \nthrough various sports promotional schemes being implemented by it. list of sports \npromotional schemes being implemented by this Ministry and the budget allocation \nfor the financial year 2018-19 is given in the statement-II (See below). All the \n\n390 Written Answers to [RAJyA sABHA] Unstarred Questions\nplay\t fields/infrastructure\t belonging\t to\t Sports\t Authority\t of\t India\t are\t of\t international\t\nstandard and are available to sportspersons.\nStatement-I\nPerformance of India in major multi-sports events\ngold silver Bronze Total\n2016 olympics games\n0 1 1 2\n2016 Paralympics games\n2 1 1 4\n2018 Commonwealth games\n26 20 20 66\n2018 Asian games\n15 24 30 69\n2018 Para Asian games\n15 24 33 72\n2018 youth olympic games\n3 9 1 13\nStatement-II\nDetails of scheme with allocation of funds for development of sports\n(` in crore)\nsl.\nNo.\nName of the scheme Budget estimate \n2018-19\n1   2 3\nA. Development in sports institutions\n1. sports Authority of India 429.56\n2. lakshmibai National Institute of Physical education 45.00\n3. National dope Test laboratory 4.00\n4. National Anti-doping Agency 10.00\n5. National Centre for sports science and Research 40.00\n6. National Centre for sports Coaching 30.00\n7. sports university in North east 65.00\n8. w orld Anti-doping Agency 1.00\nToT al  (a) 624.56\n\nWritten Answers to [11 february, 2019]   Unstarred Questions 391\n1   2 3\nB. Encouragement and awards to sportsperson\n1. special Cash Award including Rajiv gandhi Khel Ratna \nAward\n11.00\n2. Arjuna Award 1.30\n3. dhyanchand Award 0.30\n4. dronacharya Award 0.40\n5. Pension to Meritorious sportspersons 10.00\n6. Assistance to National sports federation 342.00\n7. Human Resource development in sports 5.00\n8. National sports development fund 2.00\n9. National sports w elfare fund 2.00\nToT al  (b) 374.00\nC. Khelo India-National Programme for Development of Sports\n1. Khelo India 520.09\n2. Cwg 2010-sAI stadia Renovation 0.50\n3. enhancement of sports facility at Jammu and Kashmir 50.00\n4. Himalayan Region sports festival 5.00\n5. seminar, Committee etc. 1.00\nToT al  (c) 576.59\nToT al  (a+b+c) 1575.15\nTalented sportspersons from rural background\n922. sHRI ANIl  desAI: w ill the Minister of youTH Aff AIRs ANd sPoRTs \nbe pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Chief of International Association of Athletics foundations (IAAf) \nhas stressed on importance of school sports in India;\n(b) whether India has the talented youth from rural areas to make a mark in \nthe international arena; and\n(c)\t if\t so,\t the\t adequate\t steps\t that\t Government\t is\t taking\t to\t give\t a\t fillip\t to\t the\t\nschool sports in the country, particularly in rural India?\n\n392 Written Ans. to Std. and... [RAJyA sABHA] ...the 8 February, 2019\nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe of THe MINIsTR y  of youTH Aff AIRs ANd \nsPoRTs (Col. RAJy AvARdHAN sINgH RATHoRe): (a) No formal communication \nhas been received in this Ministry recently from the Chief of International Association \nof Athletics foundations (IAAf) stressing on the importance of school sports in India.\n(b) and (c) sports is a state subject and development of sports, including \nidentification\t of\t sporting\t talent\t from\t the\t country,\t nurturing\t of\t these\t talents,\t and\t\ndevelopment of sports in schools is primarily the responsibility of the state \ngovernments and National sports federations concerned. The Central government \ncomplements/supplements their efforts in this regard. However, this Ministry, being \naware of the availability of sporting talent in the country, including rural areas, aims \nto identify and nurture them to enable them to achieve excellence in sports through \nthe vertical of “Talent search and development” of the Khelo India scheme being \nimplemented by it. The “Annual sports Competitions” vertical of the scheme provides \nthe basic platform to sportspersons from both schools and universities to showcase \ntheir sporting skills and accordingly acts as an avenue for talent spotting sporting \ntalents. Besides, the Khelo India scheme also provides for bridging critical sports \ninfrastructure gaps in the country, including in schools of rural areas.\nIn addition, sports Authority of India (sAI), an autonomous organisation under \nthe aegis of the Ministry of youth Affairs and sports, is running several sports \npromotional schemes across the country to identify talented sportspersons in the age \ngroup of 8-25 years and nurture them to excel at national and international competitions. \nMany\t of\t the\t sportspersons\t identified\t under\t SAI\t Sports\t Promotional\t Schemes\t belong\t\nto the rural, tribal, backward, coastal and inaccessible hilly areas of the country and \nare provided with training facilities in the form of expert sports coaches, requisite \nplaying facilities, boarding and lodging, sports kit, competition exposure, educational \nexpenses, medical/insurance and stipend as per the approved norm.\nWRITTEN ANSWERS TO STARRED AND UNSTARRED QUESTIONS \nSET FOR THE 8\nTH FEBRUARY, 2019 @\nInstallation of solar power projects on unused railway land\n*61. dR. AMee yAJNIK: w ill the Minister of RAIlw Ays be pleased to state:\n(a) whether government has any proposal to utilize its unused land pool for \ninstallation of solar power projects;\n@ The sitting of the Rajya sabha on friday, the 8th february, 2019 was adjourned on account of interruptions. \nAnswers\tto\tQuestions\tput\tdown\tin\tthe\tlists\tfor\tthat\tday\twere\tlaid\ton\tthe\tTable\tof\tthe\tHouse\ton\tMonday,\tthe\t11th\t\nfebruary, 2019.\n\nWritten Ans. to Std. and... [11 february, 2019]   ...the 8 February, 2019 393\n(b)\t if\t so,\t the\t detailed\tlist\tof\t nodal\tagencies\tand\t officers\tappointed\tfor\t the\t purpose;\n(c) the details about any proposal from any MNC in this regard and the progress \nmade so far; and\n(d) the details about the time-frame for the completion of the project?\nTHe MINIsTeR of RAIlw Ays (sHRI PIyusH goy Al): (a) and (b) yes, sir. \nMinistry of Railways is planning for installation of solar panels on unutilized Railway \nland for meeting its energy needs for both traction and non-traction purpose. The \nNodal Agency for execution of this project is yet to be decided. Nodal directorate \nunder Ministry of Railways is electrical energy Management directorate. so far, Indian \nRailways has already set up 77.99 Mega w att (Mw) of solar Power Plants (74.99 \nMw  on rooftops and 3 Mw  on land) and planning/execution is further under progress \nfor 176.46 Mw  of rooftop capacity and 54 Mw  of land based solar power plants.\n(c) There is no such proposal from any MNC.\n(d) Indian Railways plans to meet its power requirement progressively through \nsolar power.\nAllocation of Microwave Access Spectrum\n*62. sHRI RA vI PRAKAsH veRMA: w ill the Minister of CoMMuNICATIoNs  \nbe pleased to state:\n(a) whether serious irregularities in allocation of Microwave Access spectrum in \n2015 have been reported by CAg recently;\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether government has initiated inquiry into the alleged irregularities to \nfix\t responsibility;\n(d) if so, the details thereof; and\n(e) if not, the reasons therefor?\nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe of THe MINIsTR y  of CoMMuNICATIoNs \n(sHRI MANoJ sINHA): (a) and (b) There are no irregularities in allocation of \nMicrowave Access spectrum. However, Comptroller and Auditor general (CAg) have \nobserved the following:–\n “Thus, Audit is of the view that allotment of Mw A carriers to TsPs should \nbe made equitably and through market related process.”\n\n394 Written Ans. to Std. and... [RAJyA sABHA] ...the 8 February, 2019\nso far, Microwave backhaul carriers have been allotted only through administrative \nprocess.\n(c) to (e) Not applicable in view of (a) to (b) above.\nNote: Mw A stands for Microwave Access and TsPs stands for Telecom service \nProviders.\nNon-disbursement of MSP to farmers\n*63. sHRI RIPuN BoRA: w ill the Minister of AgRICul TuRe  ANd f ARMe Rs  \nwelf ARe be pleased to state: \n(a) whether it is a fact that the farmers in the country are still unable to repay \nloans due to non-receiving of MsP in the country; \n(b) if so, the details of Central support of MsP to farmers for the period  \n2016-17, 2017-18 and April to december, 2018, crop-wise;\n(c) the disbursement of MsPs to farmers during the said periods; and \n(d) the action taken by government to safeguard the interests of the farmers?\nTHe MINIsTeR of AgRICul TuRe ANd f ARMeRs welf ARe (sHRI RAdHA \nMoHAN sINgH): (a) sir, there is no such information.\n(b) and (c) do not arise. However, the crop-wise details of procurement made \nfrom farmers at MsP for the period 2016-17, 2017-18 and April to december, \n2018 are given in statement-I, II, III and Iv  respectively (See below). for these \nprocurement, farmers have been granted MsP for their produce. \n(d) In order to ensure Minimum support Price (MsP) to farmers an umbrella \nscheme of “Pradhan Mantri Annadata Aay sanraksHan Abhiyan” (PM-AAsHA), \ncomprising\t Price\t Support\t Scheme\t (PSS),\t Price\t Deficiency\t Payment\t Scheme\t (PDPS),\t\nand pilot of Private Procurement and stockist scheme (PPss) and existing schemes \nof department of food and Public distribution and Ministry of Textiles. \nfurther, for transparent price discovery to get remunerative prices for the \nfarmers for their produce through competitive online bidding system, government is \nimplementing National Agriculture Market (e-NAM) scheme. In order to optimize the \nuse of scarce resources and mitigate the uncertainty in price and marketing, government \nhas formulated and released a progressive and facilitative Model Act “The–state/uT \nAgricultural Produce and livestock Contract farming and services (Promotion and \nfacilitation) Act, 2018” in May, 2018 for its adoption by the states/union Territories \n\nWritten Ans. to Std. and... [11 february, 2019]   ...the 8 February, 2019 395\n(uTs). The aforesaid Model Contract farming Act covers the entire value and supply \nchain from pre-production to post harvest marketing including services contract for \nthe agricultural produce and livestock. further, In order to provide better marketing \nfacilities to the farmers, the government has released a new model “The Agricultural \nProduce and livestock Marketing (Promotion and facilitation) Act, 2017” in April, \n2017 for its adoption by states/uTs. The model act provides for alternative marketing \nchannels such as setting up of private markets, direct marketing, farmer-consumer \nmarkets, special commodity markets, to facilitate farmers in marketing their produce at \ncompetitive and remunerative prices. To develop Agricultural Marketing Infrastructure \nincluding storage infrastructure, government is implementing capital investment subsidy \nsub-scheme “Agricultural Marketing Infrastructure (AMI)” of Integrated scheme for \nAgricultural Marketing (IsAM) with two distinct marketing infrastructure components \neither (i) storage Infrastructure in rural area, and (ii) other than storage infrastructure.\nStatement-I\nDetails of pulses and oilseeds procured at MSP under PSS and PSF during \n2016-17, 2017-18 and 2018-19 (April to December, 2018)\nyear/Commodity MsP (` Per MT) Quantity\t Procured\t\n(in MTs)\nMsP Cost \n(` in lakh)\n1 2 3 4\n2016-17\nMilling Copra 59500 4488.94 2670.92\nBall Copra 62400 1836.86 1146.20\ngroundnut 42200 210731.16 88928.55\nMoong 52250 219431.23 114652.82\nsoyabean 27750 162.19 45.01\nSunflower\t Seed\t 38000 4949.31 1880.74\nToor 50500 1353095.52 683313.24\nToT al  1794695.21 892637.47\n2017-18\ngroundnut-Rabi 42200 947.77 399.96\ngroundnut-Kharif 44500 1049136.91 466865.92\nMoong-Rabi 52250 112405.99 58732.13\nMoong-Kharif 55750 294903.19 164408.53\n\n396 Written Ans. to Std. and... [RAJyA sABHA] ...the 8 February, 2019\n1 2 3 4\nMustard seed 37000 36940.18 13667.87\nsesamum seed 50000 3419.81 1709.91\nsoyabean 30500 72282.10 22046.04\nSunflower\t Seed\t 39500 6539.09 2582.94\nToor 54500 873758.62 476198.45\nurad-Rabi 54000 276666.25 149399.78\nurad-Kharif 50000 15747.65 7873.83\nToT al  2742747.56 1363885.34\n2018-19\ngram 44000 2769430.16 1218549.27\ngroundnut-Rabi 44500 2660.01 1183.70\ngroundnut-Kharif 48900 360810.29 176436.23\nMasoor 42500 246943.85 104951.14\nMoong-Rabi 55750 4279.16 2385.63\nMoong-Kharif 69750 259723.32 181157.02\nMustard seed 40000 873661.00 349464.40\nNigerseed 58770 0.40 0.24\nsoyabean 33990 18771.93 6380.58\nSunflower\t Seed\t 41000 2745.43 1125.63\nToor 56750 8171.70 4637.44\nurad-Rabi 54000 86927.63 46940.92\nurad-Kharif 56000 237206.37 132835.57\nToT al  4871331.25 2226047.76\ng rand  