 measures taken to start the above railway line by government \nin 2019?\nTHe MINIsTeR of RAIlw Ays (sHRI PIyusH goy Al): (a) y es, sir. \nsakri-Jhanjharpur-Nirmali (51 Kms), Jhanjharpur- l aukaha Bazar (43 Kms) gauge \nConversion sections are part of sakri-Jhanjharpur-Nirmali, Jhanjharpur-laukaha Bazar \nand saharsa-sarayagarh-forbesganj (206 Kms) gauge Conversion project. This project \nwas sanctioned in 2003-04. detailed estimate amounting to ` 1470.50 crore has been \nsanctioned for execution of this project. execution of work on entire section has been \ntaken up. Total expenditure of ` 457.44 crore has been incurred upto March, 2018. \nAn outlay of ` 200\t crore\t has\t been\t made\t for\t the\t financial\t year\t 2018-19.\n(b) Total expenditure on sakri-Jhanjharpur-Nirmali (51 Kms), Jhanjharpur-l aukaha \nBazar (43 Kms) and saharsa-sarayagarh-forbesganj (112 Kms) gauge Conversion \nproject from 2003-04 to 2013-14 was only ` 285 crore since 2014-15 onwards, \nbudget allotment for this project has been enhanced and expenditure of ` 172.44 \ncrore has been incurred till March, 2018 and an outlay of ` 200 crore has been \ngiven in 2018-19.\n(c) This project is located in North Bihar and passes through six districts of \ndarbhanga, Madhubani, saharsa, supaul, Araria and Madhepura. People residing in \nthese\t areas\t will\t be\t benefitted\t by\t this\t project.\n(d) By close monitoring of the project and enhanced allotment of funds, execution \nof work has been expedited. gauge Conversion of sakri-Jhanjharpur-Nirmali (51 Kms) \nand saharsa-sarayagarh (52 Kms) sections are planned to be commissioned in 2019.\nAssistance to distressed coconut growers of Kerala\n*65. sHRI v. MuRAleedHARAN: w ill the Minister of AgRICul TuRe ANd \nf ARMeRs welf ARe be pleased to state: \n(a) the steps initiated by government to assist the coconut growers in distress \nin Kerala due to sudden fall in procurement price of coconut in recent months, if \nso, the details thereof; and \n(b) the steps taken by government to support and encourage coconut growers \nin\t the\t country\t along\t with\t the\t details\t of\t the\t amount\t allocated\t during\t the\t last\t five\t\nyears for the coconut growers, state-wise?\n\n404 Written Ans. to Std. and... [RAJyA sABHA] ...the 8 February, 2019\nTHe MINIsTeR of AgRICul TuRe ANd f ARMeRs welf ARe (sHRI RAdHA \nMoHAN sINgH): (a) The average wholesale price of coconut was ruling at ` 17-19/- \nper nut during 2018 which comes to around `  38/- per kg. The Minimum support \nPrice (MsP) of de-husked coconut was ` 2030/- per quintal for the season 2018. The \nprice of coconut prevailing in the market was about 95-114% higher than the MsP \ndeclared for de-husked coconut. The MsP declared for milling copra for the season \n2018 was `  7,511/- per quintal, whereas the average price of milling copra prevailing \nin the market was ` 11,810/- per quintal. The MsP of ball copra for the season \n2018 was `  7,750/- per quintal whereas the average price of ball copra prevailing in \nthe market was `  15,060/- per quintal. Hence, the proposal for procurement of de-\nhusked coconut, milling copra and ball copra under Price support scheme (Pss) was \nnot received from any of the states/union Territories including Kerala. The monthly \naverage price of coconut and milling copra in Kerala markets during the year 2018 \nis given in statement-I (See below). \nHowever, in order to support the small holder coconut farmers and increase their \nbargaining power, the Coconut development Board (CdB), Kochi has formed farmer \ncollectives with Coconut Producer societies (CPss) at grass root level comprising of \n40-100 coconut farmers in a contiguous area, Coconut Producer federations (CPfs) \nat intermediary level comprising of 8-10 CPs and Coconut Producer Companies \n(CPCs) at the apex level formed by combining 8 to 10 CPfs which are registered \nunder Indian Companies Act of 2013.\nThe fPos are undertaking collective marketing of coconut, processing of coconut \nto copra and coconut oil, and production of other value added products from coconut \nlike\t neera\t beverage,\t sugar,\t honey,\t jaggery\t etc.\t CDB\t has\t till\t date\t extended\t financial\t\nsupport to fPos for establishment of 32 copra drying units, 5 coconut oil processing \nunits and 11 neera processing units. Through this initiative, farmers are able to realize \nbetter\t prices\t and\t the\t benefit\t of\t value\t addition\t reaches\t the\t grass\t root\t level\t farmer.\n(b) government, through Coconut development Board (C dB), has been \nimplementing various schemes such as production and distribution of quality planting \nmaterials, expansion of area under coconut, integrated farming in coconut holding \nfor productivity improvement, technology demonstration/quality testing laboratory, \nmarketing, market intelligence services, statistics and strengthening of export Promotion \nCouncil, information and information technology, technology mission on coconut, \nreplanting and rejuvenation of coconut gardens, coconut palm insurance scheme and \nKera suraksha Insurance scheme, for the welfare of coconut farmers in the country. \nThe\t amount\t allocated\t during\t the\t last\t five\t years\t for\t the\t coconut\t growers,\t State-wise,\t\nis given in statement-II.\n\nWritten Ans. to Std. and... [11 february, 2019]   ...the 8 February, 2019 405\nStatement-I\nMonthly average price of coconut and copra in Kerala markets \nduring the year 2018\n(A) Monthly average price of coconut in Kerala markets during the year 2018\n(` per 1000 nuts)\nMonths/year Trivandrum Market Alappuzha Market\nJanuary 25000 18600\nfebruary 24750 18600\nMarch 22400 17868\nApril 23000 17977\nMay 22500 17980\nJune 19150 17550\nJuly 16938 17332\nAugust 16750 17297\nseptember 16275 16997\noctober 15000 16235\nNovember 14300 15663\ndecember 16313 16797\na verage 19365 17408\nSource:\t Economics\tand\tStatistics,\tDistrict\tOffice,\tThiruvanathapuram,\tDirecto