\n(d) An Inter-Ministerial Central Team (IMCT) visited the drought affected areas \nof\t the\t State\t during\t 5th\t to\t 7th\t December,\t 2018.\t Based\t on\t the\t findings\t of\t the\t IMCT\t\nand the recommendations of the sub-Committee of National executive Committee \n(sC-NeC), the High level Committee (HlC) in its meeting held on 29.01.2019, has \nalready approved ` 900.40 crore from NdRf to Andhra Pradesh for drought Kharif \n2018. Hence, there has been no delay.\n\nWritten Ans. to Std. and... [11 february, 2019]   ...the 8 February, 2019 423\nStatement\nDistrict-wise names of mandals in Andhra Pradesh declared as drought-affected\nsl.No. district No. of Mandals Mandals\n1. Kadapa 51 Kondapuram, Mylavaram, Peddamudium, Rajupalem, duvvur, s. Mydukur, Brahmamgarimatham, \nsri Avadhuta Kasinayana, Porumamilla, B. Kodur, Badvel, gopavaram, Khajipet, Chapadu, \nProddatur, Jammalamadugu, Muddanur, simhadripuram, lingala, Pulivendula, v emula, \nThondur, v eerapanayani Palle, yerraguntla, Kamalapuram, vallur, Chennur, Atlur, v ontimitta, \nsidhout, Kadapa, Chinthakomma dinne, Pendlimarri, vempalle, Chakrayapet, galiveedu, \nChinnamandem, sambepalle, T sundupalle, Rayachoti, l akkireddipalle, Ramapuram, veeraballi, \nPenagalur, Chitvel, Rajampet, Pullampeta, obulavaripalle, Koduru, Nandalur, Kalasapadu\n2. Ananthapuram 63 v idapanakal, guntakal, gooty, y adiki, Peddapappur, singanamala, galadinne, Kudair, \nuravakonda, Beluguppa, Kanekal, Rayadurg, settur, Rayadurg, Ananatapur, Bukkaraya \nsamudram, Narpala, Putlur, y ellanur, Tadimarri, Bathalapalle, Raptadu, Kanaganapalle, \nKambadur, Ramagiri, dharmavaram, Mudigubba, Talupula, Nambulipulikunta, Tanakal, \nNallacheruvu, gandlapenta, Kadiri, obuladevaracheruvu, Nallamda, Puttaparthi, \nBukkapatnam, Kothacheruvu, Penukonda, Roddam, somandepallli, Chilamathur, Parigi, Agali, \nBrahmasamudram, Bommanahal, d.Hirehal, gorantla, gudibanda, gummagatta, Hindupur, \nKundurpi, l epakshi, Madakasira, Pamidi, Peddavadugur, R