and Banana\n697. sHRI v. MuRAleedHARAN: w ill the Minister of food PRoCessINg \nINdusTRIes be pleased to state:\n(a) whether government has received any proposals for setting up food processing \nunits for jackfruit and banana from Kerala, Tamil Nadu and Karnataka; and\n(b) whether government plans to use the potential of these fruits for food \nprocessing industries?\nTHe MINIsTeR of sTATe IN THe MINIsTR y  of food PRoCessINg \nINdusTRI es (sAdHvI NIRANJAN JyoTI): (a) Ministry of food Processing \nIndustries (MofPI) has received and approved one proposal namely of M/s Jaycee \norganics llP located at survey No. 119/4C, udayampuli v illage, Alangulam TK, \nTirunelveli district for setting up of fruit and vegetable processing unit including \njackfruit and banana from the state of Tamil Nadu. However, no proposal for jackfruit \nor banana processing has been received from the states of Kerala and Karnataka.\n(b) Ministry of food Processing Industries (MofPI) is implementing a scheme for \nCreation/expansion of food Processing and Preservation Capacities (CefPPC) under \nthe Pradhan Mantri Kisan sampada yojana (PMKsy) for setting up/expansion of food \nprocessing industries including fruits and vegetables processing units in the country. \nunder the scheme, grants-in-aid @ 35% of the eligible project cost is provided in \ngeneral Areas and 50% of the eligible project cost in North eastern states including \nSikkim\t and\t Difficult\tareas\t including\t Himalayan\t States\t (Himachal\t Pradesh,\t Jammu\t and\t\nKashmir\t and\t Uttarakhand),\t notified\t ITDP\t areas\t and\t Islands\t subject\t to\t a\t maximum\t\nof ` 5.00 crore.\nThe food processing units, including fruits and vegetables processing units, \ncan be set up in Mega food Parks (MfPs), Agro Processing Clusters (APCs) and \nDesignated\t Food\t Parks\t (DFPs)\t notified\t by\t the\t Ministry\t from\t time\t to\t time.\t However,\t\nin states/uTs without any MfP, APC or dfP, the food processing units may be \nsetup anywhere in the state/uT.\nfurther, the units having majority stake of sC/sT promoter(s) and with an eligible \nproject cost of more than ` \t 5\t (five)\tcrore\t can\t be\t set\t up\t at\t any\t location\tin\t the\t country.\nMofPI has invited online proposals under the scheme for setting up of food \nProcessing units including for these fruits in the country. The closing date for \nsubmission of online proposals is 31.03.2019.The interested entrepreneurs may submit \ntheir proposal on line.\nHowever, the details of food processing units including for fruits and vegetables \napproved in the states of Kerala, Tamil Nadu and Karnataka are given in statement.\n\n596 Written Ans. to Std. and... [RAJyA sABHA] ...the 8 February, 2019\nStatement\nDetails of food processing units including fruits and vegetables processing units approved in the States of Kerala, Tamil Nadu \nand Karnataka under the scheme for Creation/Expansion of Food Processing and Preservation Capacities (CEFPPC)  \nof Pradhan Mantri Kisan Sampada Yojana (PMKSY)\n(` in crore)\nsl. \nNo.\nName of the applicant location of the project/district sector date of\nApproval\nTotal \nProject \nCost\nApproved \ngrants-in- \naid\nReleased \ngrants-in- \naid\n1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8\nKerala\n1. M/s Protech organo foods \nPvt. ltd.\nKsI dC Mega food Park, Pallippuram \nv illage Cherthala\nfish and Marine \nProcessing\n19.02.2018 20.35 4.91 0\n2. M/s Cacobean Chocolate \nfactory Pvt. ltd.\nKINfRA small Industrial Park, v illage \nMuzhavanoor, Taluk Kunnathunadu\nConsumer Products 26.09.2018 14.86 4.28 0\n3. M/s Anthocyanin Naturals \nIndia Pvt. ltd.\nKINfRA Mega food Park, v illage \nelappully\nConsumer Products \n(oleoresin and essential \noils)\n09.01.2019 18.77 3.63 0\n4. M/s Maak Natural extractors \nPvt. ltd.\nKINfRA Mega food Park, v illage \nelappully\nConsumer Products \n(oleoresin and essential \noils)\n31.01.2019 17.86 4.51 0\n Tamil Nadu\n1. M/s Neo foods Pvt. ltd. devaganpalli, denkanikotta Taluk f&v  Proce